          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "నీరసం (nīrasaṁ) — \"weakness, lethargy\", the drained feeling after a fever."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "నాకు నీరసంగా ఉంది — \"I feel weak\", in the frame of అలసటగా and దాహంగా."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "నీరసం (nīrasaṁ) is Sanskrit nīrasa, \"sapless, tasteless\", taken over whole as a learned loan, a tatsama, with the Telugu noun ending -ṁ (CDIAL 7556). The sense \"weakness\" is the one Telugu gives it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A cold, medicine, a hospital, a wound, weakness: enough for a visit to the doctor."
            }
          ]
        },
